{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/405353-weather-and-its-effects-in-the-shadowlands","id":405353,"title":"Weather and its effects in the Shadowlands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-13T17:57:03-08:00","id":405353,"title":"Weather and its effects in the Shadowlands","content":"Good evening gents!<br /> <br /> I've been reading the 2nd edition Wraith book, and I gotta say I'm freaking fascinated with the theme.<br /> <br /> Though I wanted to ask, are there weather changes in the Shadowlands? I'm aware that the Tempest is, well, a tempest with all sorts of crazy weather effects going on, but no mention about the Shadowlands having weather in the books is made.<br /> <br /> And I know that, if I want to, I can create weather effects in the Shadowlands, but I wonder if it would be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5017-awildmann","name":"AWildmann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T21:46:09-08:00","id":405455,"title":"","content":"I think it is totally appropriate to have &quot;weather&quot; in the Shadowlands as long as you remember that &quot;weather&quot; there is different than it is in the Skinlands. Weather has an emotional, spiritual, and fatalistic component in the Shadowlands. Bad &quot;storms&quot; are low level maelstroms, so even lesser kinds of weather should have some sort of meaning or omen, even if it is not understood.<br /> <br /> So if you need a certain kind of weather to create the proper kind of mood, or to serve as a theme for the game session, go right ahead!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T00:12:28-08:00","id":405507,"title":"","content":"Weather in the Shadowlands (unless it's emerged from the Tempest and is purely on the Shadowland side of the Shroud,, like the maelstroms Black Fox mentioned) is generally purely cosmetic, a combination of what's going on in the Skinlands visible across the Shroud but not shredding through a Wraith's corpus (droplets of water or snow does not force you incorporeal to move uninterrupted by your presence), as warped in appearance by the emotional and entropic aspects of the Shadowlands like everything else.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T02:17:01-08:00","id":405608,"title":"","content":"As the shadowlands is more or less a reflection of the skinlands... if it is raining in the skinlands, it is raining in the shadowlands. Per the &quot;rule of ouch&quot; the rain wouldn't affect wraiths much, and would probably pass right through them, without having to go incorporeal.<br /> <br /> Maelstroms are something altogether different. Basically, the tempest bursts forth into the shadowlands (or anywhere else the tempest touches) bringing with it a torrent of spectres, relic debris, rains of plasm or soulfire all accompanied by hurricane-force wind.<br /> <br /> Maelstroms are one reason for the creation of citadels, which serve as a public shelter against the maelstrom. Haunts are also valued as shelters.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Great Maelstroms, which occur in times of great death and destruction. There have been 5 (or 6) Great Maelstroms, ever, and each was worse than the last. GM6 was so bad it brought about the end of the wraith line. As far as Wraith is concerned, GM6 never ended... I never read Orpheus, but they may have something else to say on the matter.<br /> <br /> GM1: The Fall of Rome<br /> GM2: Black Plague<br /> GM3: Conquest of the Americas<br /> GM4: WWI, Spanish Flu<br /> GM5: WWII, Nagasaki, Hiroshima, Holocaust<br /> GM6: Relic Nukes set off in Enoch and the Labyrinth, War between Dark Kingdoms of Iron and Jade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 02-14-2015, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T12:01:49-08:00","id":406881,"title":"","content":"As it's the shadowlands I agree with the above that weather is appropriate.<br /> Was it just ordinary weather like fog and rain you had in mind or some freak weather conditions unique to the shadowlands?<br /> For example I could see some very weird showers of plasmic frogs that could inconvenience the everyday lives of a citadel or ball lightning that giggles like a small child before exploding.<br /> But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>I'm God's hated messenger, the Devil's cohort<br /> I'm the one they all blame, when a life is cut short<br /> But still if you're willing, to give it a try<br /> I'll beat you at anything, and claim you're last sigh</i><br /> - The Reaper's Tales","edited":{"userid":4688,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4688-malkira","user":"Malkira","date":". 02-16-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4688-malkira","name":"Malkira","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:57:44-08:00","id":407948,"title":"","content":"I remember a sketch in one of the sourcebooks showing a rain of broken glass. I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:44:45-08:00","id":408445,"title":"","content":"Shrapnel keeps falling on my head,<br /> But that doesn't mean my eyes would be turning red,<br /> How could this be,<br /> Because I drive a KV.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:50:07-08:00","id":424547,"title":"","content":"As a game where the subject is hunted by their own fetters, haunted by their own shadow, and traumatized by some horrific event to create them - the perception of weather may be a very individualistic condition. Three wraiths sitting together may simultaneously each experience a completely different environment - in their head.<br /> <br /> Consider the weather of a business man who has been taken for everything he had and left as the scapegoat not only for a murder he didn't commit but a paper trail connects him to acts of treason. He doesn't even know who has framed him. In a stupor he leaves the building, crosses the street through the cool drizzle, and sits on a bench. Thunder peels and the cool drizzle shifts instantly to pounding near freezing rain. Physically near catatonic, his mind races - aches - explodes into near suffocation in a caul, as his hear slowly, ever so slowly ... beats and stays forever silent. The rain is an element of his death. It is not merely the fact of what happened when he died, but symbolic of the down pour of bad in his last moments of life. His clothes are always cold and wet. His feet always track water with traces of ectoplasmic mud. He is forever shivering in the rain, and cannot for some reason ever seem to get an umbrella that works.<br /> <br /> Another wraith sees the Shadowlands as that last sunny picnic where stressed and depressed from abuse, some might even say deranged, she fed her violent husband and silent children the tuna salad sandwiches she laced with fresh hemlock. She frolicks with her children under the loving gaze of her husband - a family eternally together in the afternoon sun of Mother's Day.<br /> <br /> The third, was a middle aged curmudgeonly sort who at age 36 had still never been on a date, shot in the back of the head in his cubicle. He dies the victim of a customer who does not want such scrutiny of his finances. The accountant is still working on that accounting problem that just wouldn't balance. The sunset in the window across the way the only touch of light and life he ever saw - the side note of his 15 to 18 hour days. Still working in his central air environment, he continues to work - and the sunset, like his life, remains just over there, out of focus, almost out of sight, just like the life he never had.<br /> <br /> All three of these wraiths sit together, members of the same legion, each dying in that last moment. Each carrying with them the experience of their death, the value of their unresolved life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:24:04-08:00","id":424596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/405353-weather-and-its-effects-in-the-shadowlands?p=405507#post405507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weather in the Shadowlands (unless it's emerged from the Tempest and is purely on the Shadowland side of the Shroud,, like the maelstroms Black Fox mentioned) is generally purely cosmetic, a combination of what's going on in the Skinlands visible across the Shroud but not shredding through a Wraith's corpus (droplets of water or snow does not force you incorporeal to move uninterrupted by your presence), as warped in appearance by the emotional and entropic aspects of the Shadowlands like everything else.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> I don't see things as being super-subjective on a wraith by wraith basis. That's more Harrowings and Transcendence. <br /> <br /> Or rains of glass, tears and blood, pooling on the ground as used needles and lost ballpoints pens. Those seem more like the Tempest and Maelstroms.<br /> <br /> Life as a wraith is in a grey and dreary world. The sunlight is bleached out, washing out what it touches, but not illuminating quite as much as it would in the Skinlands. Rain hisses flatly, never cheerfully pattering. Etc. Etc. There might be a few temporal offsets.... as the Skinland storm dies down , it begins to pick up across the Shroud... the analogue storm growing stronger as it's &quot;living&quot; counterpart &quot;dies', etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:30:39-08:00","id":424735,"title":"","content":"Could be worse. Like for our recently deceased lady here.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KHjXMGOhRUA\" data-code=\"KHjXMGOhRUA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/KHjXMGOhRUA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}